According to the handbook for the KZPCA-AA it is a '16 bit LVD and  SE
solution' and also supports legacy Fast SCSI and Ultra SCSI devices.

When the system boots up a message is displayed for  SCSI controller
PKB stating 'Operating mode is SE Ultra SCSI' which I think is correct
for the TLZ10 and the external disks.
SCSI controller PKA, connected to the system disk only, reports
'operating mode is LVD Ultra SCSI'
I gather that the controllers automatically configure to whatever mode
is compatible with all connected devices.

The internal SCSI cables have terminators on them and 16 bit
termination is enabled on the BA356 i/o module.

All devices have unique id's - see device names below:

TLZ10 = MKB400

External disk #1 = DKB100
External disk #2 = DKB200

Internal System disk = DKA0



