>I have found that if I connect the TLZ10 on the same SCSI bus as the 2
>external hdd's I get a crop of block verify errors when I transfer
>files between the hdd's using the �backup/verify�' command.
>These do not occur if I disconnect the TLZ10
>
>However, if I connect the TLZ10 on the same bus as the internal hdd
>instead and do similar things on this hdd I do not get the problem.

Some of the older DEC SCSI controllers have both internal and external
connections, but using both of them at the same time is not supported.  

It's possible that it could me made to work.  That would mean that the
controller is in the middle of the bus, and you would have to turn off the
controller's terminator somehow.  I think you can do this from the SRM
console:

>>>SET PKB0_TERMPWR 0

And of course you would terminate the far ends of the internal and external
chains.

