When you turn it on, it should first run some diagnostics,
and show various letters and numbers on the 1st line of the screen
it also beeps a number of times if thing fail
(you will have to get the owners guide mentioned above for full details)
It should also identify it's firmware version.
If you can get your hands on an alpha firmware cd, then this has 
the latest versions for (nearly) all models.
If your firmware is not the latest, then update it.
You may also need an "ECU" disk, mentioned by a previous poster.
