Patrick, as all have said, this error is related to the graphics adapter 
embedded on the Flamingo/3000-500.  I had two "bird" systems (one a 500, 
the other a 500X) that got these errors and ran for a LONG time.  As 
long as you're getting console output to the monitor and you get a 
decent DECwindows startup when booting VMS, you can limp along with this 
for a while.  The biggest nuisance is the system won't boot without 
intervention after a powerfail, so someone has to force it past the 
error to get it booted.

You might also try upgrading the firmware on the system, some more 
recent versions mentioned that some CXT errors were fixed there.  If you 
have spare cables and/or monitors that can be swapped, you might give 
those a try too.

bob



