:So for the dongle like thing i have: It is defenitedly no SCSI-terminator.
:But i noticed that the printer port on the DEC3000/300 is not really a 
:parallelport but the serialport with a male subD 25. That is also where
:the dongle like thing fits on. When i am at home, i think i do a photo
:of it, there is also a number on the back.

  Guess: 29-24795; a serial loopback, used for console serial line and
  system diagnostic testing.

  There are other DB25 adapters for MMJ connections, for instance, and many 
  of these adapters are listed in the OpenVMS FAQ.

  The DEC 3000 series is sufficently old that it uses the DIGITAL classic
  I/O connectors, rather than the PC-centric connectors.  This means the
  keyboard, mouse, serial lines, etc.  Parallel ports didn't make widespread
  appearances until the PC-centric I/O arrived, and that post-dated this box.
  It's also old enough that it probably has the old synch-on-green video
  connection, rather than one of the more common PC video connections.
  Various of this stuff has been discussed before, and there are pointers
  and such in the OpenVMS FAQ.


