>SCSI was what crossed mine mind for it.  I have some free scsi ports on 
>both the dec 3000�s

You can't make a VMS cluster with only SCSI for the interconnect.  The
only cluster interconnects available for the DEC 3000 systems are ethernet
and FDDI.

Even with a supported cluster interconnect, you can't share the on-board
SCSI between multiple systems.  The controller lacks advanced SCSI
features such as target mode.  The only turbochannel SCSI adapter that
supports shared SCSI in VMS clusters is the KZTSA.


