On Sat, 9 Aug 2003, Jeroen M.W. van Dijk wrote:

> For the DECstation 5000/2xx series you must use all MS02-AA (8MB memory 
> modules) or all MS02-CA (32MB memory modules) in a workstation. There are 
> 15 memory banks on these systems. You can not intermix the memory module 
> types on the same machine. When using MS02-AA memory, the maximum is 120MB 
> per workstation. The maximum is 480MB when MS02-CA memory modules are used. 

 Actually you *can* mix MS02 memory module types -- this is fully
supported both by the hardware and by the firmware.  When mixing module
types, the module in the first slot has to be a 32MB MS02-CA.  Others may
be arranged arbitrarily. 

 Such a configuration might not necessarily be supported by various
operating systems.  Specifically, Ultrix only supports a single 8MB module
at the end of a set of 32MB ones, Linux supports any configuration and
NetBSD -- well, I don't know.

