You knock vi, but it is the only editor you can be 100% sure will be
usable on any UNIX system. Emacs, textedit etc are fine, but what if
/usr/local won't mount ? What if one of the many libraries they need
is corrupted ? What if .... etc etc.  

I'm not a wizard at vi at all - know just a few basic commands, but it
is still my preference of an editor. Even if you don't like vi, you
should know how to use it, because one day you might have no other
choice, when a system is seriously broken. If any editor will allow
you to escape from jail, it will be vi. 


