> someone fill me in as to what I did wrong??!?! Wrong newsgroup? Too
> tough a question? Not enough participation on my part? Bad
> 'Netiquette'?? Please help me understand
> 
> David

Ah, so little faith :-). If loopback works ok, then it's probably safe
to assume that the terminal works. Dec systems are usually set up to use
data leads only, with xon/xoff flow control, so modem control lines
should be ignored.

It's been some time, but make sure you have the terminal menus (F3,
IIRC) set for data leads only, xon/xoff flow control, interpret controls
and that the baud rate, stop bits (1), parity (none), data bits (8) are
correct. Some dec terminals support split baud rates, so make sure they
are the same on tx and rx.

Otherwise, it looks like a simple hardware cable problem, especially as
you say that you can talk data one way with another terminal. A good
idea would be to get hold of the correct dec terminal mmj cable if you
are not already using one. The terminal manual should tell you which one
to use...

Chris


