It may have helped to report what kind of server you are connecting to.
Also, when you shorted pins 2-5, was it at the vt420 MMJ connector or on the
other end of the cable at the server?  You didn't say whether one of your
other terminals works okay plugged into the same wire you are trying to get
the 420 to work on.  If you are connecting to a DEC VAX or Alpha running
VMS, there are some tests you can do from the console to help isolate the
problem.  If you are using x-on/x-off flow control, then you may simply need
to do a Ctrl-Q to unlock the flow.  If you are using hardware flow control,
you have to make sure both the server and the terminal is getting a clear to
send voltage.  Since you are using non-DEC terminals elsewhere, I am
thinking that they have a DB25 comm connector, and you are using some kind
of MMJ to DB25 adapter at the 420.  What is the part number?  It could be
the wrong type or it could be defective.  From the statement that you
connected to a Link terminal and didn't receive anything on the 420, but you
can get a loopback to work, that sounds like a bad cable.  You didn't say
whether you had a known-good cable.

So, to answer your question about why nobody jumped in to help, the lack of
detail is sometimes a turnoff to potential helpers because it becomes a long
string of questions and answers to get a clear picture of your setup, even
before the troubleshooting can begin.

If you can answer all these questions, you will have a better chance at a
response.  Hope that helps.


