  -- Robert


Notes from "DEC 3000 Model 500/500S AXP Service Information"
Order number EK-FLAMI-SV.C01
March 1993


OVERVIEW
The CXT diagnostic ensures the integrity of the graphics
subsystem and monitor.


RUNNING CXT DIAGNOSTICS
To run the CXT diagnostics, use the TEST command:

>>> T CXT [subtest][?][-v][-d][-cn][-b][-m][-wr][-nc]


QUALIFIERS
You can specify the following qualifiers with the CXT diagnostic:

Qualifier      Meaning
?        Lists available subtests.
-v       Verbose qualifier, for stepping through a test.
-d       Keeps the display active.
-cn      Font qualifier, where n is the font character.
-b       Scrolls black characters on a white background.
-m       Specifies the multinational font set (8-bit).
-wr      Specifies the number of rows (r) to stipple.
-nl      Specifies the number of lines (l) in a quadrant.
-wr      Specifies the number of rows (r) to copy (copy test).

ERROR REPORTING
The diagnostic reports any error that it finds. Error messages
include a hexadecimal longword of data and an FRU code to
identify the failing FRU:

>>> TEST CXT
?? 001 CXT XXXXXXXX

The FRU for all graphics failures is the system module, since that's where
the graphics hardware is soldered in.

