I don't know of any current VMS firewall software.  I guess you could
build your own with some work.

To make a VMS cluster with these systems, you'd need them on a common
ethernet segment.  If you have an add-on ethernet adapter for one system,
the extra network port could be connected to the outside world.  TCPIP
services for VMS has some routing capabilities.

Turbochannel ethernet adapters are PMAD-AA.  Same capabilities as the
built-in network on the DEC 3000 systems, except the PMAD only has an AUI
connector.  You might find PMAD modules cheap at ebay or other used
equipment dealers.


