For the DECstation 5000/2xx series you must use all MS02-AA (8MB memory 
modules) or all MS02-CA (32MB memory modules) in a workstation. There are 
15 memory banks on these systems. You can not intermix the memory module 
types on the same machine. When using MS02-AA memory, the maximum is 120MB 
per workstation. The maximum is 480MB when MS02-CA memory modules are used. 
When ordering memory for the DECstation 5000/2xx series make sure you are 
matching the memory type already installed in your workstation. 

  DECstation 5000 model 200, 240, 260 (all are one SIMM sets)
      MS02-AA   8MB
      MS02-CA  32MB

For the DECstation 5000/xx and DECstation 5000/1xx series you must install 
all MS01-AA (4MB memory modules) or all MS01-CA (16MB memory modules) in 
the workstation. The 5000/xx systems have 8MB built-in on the motherboard 
plus two memory banks. The 5000/1xx systems have eight memory banks. You 
cannot intermix the different memory modules on the same machine. A 
DECstation 5000/25 will hold a maximum of 16MB using 4MB modules, and 40MB 
using 16MB modules. DECstation 5000/1xx workstations will hold a maximum of 
32MB using 4MB modules and 128MB using 16MB modules. 

http://trouble.iastate.edu/pvmembuy.htm

There seems to be also MS02-BA modules out there, but they are very rare.
A pair is 20 MB. They are upgrade MS02-AA modules.

