I experimented with Redhat Linux (Alpha distribution) on a PW 500au, for the
purpose of running an Xvnc server.  It was very easy to install the OS.  But
the Pentium binaries are not compatible, so I had to download sources for
all the software I wanted.  No problem, the Alpha gcc compiler is *very*
fast.

In the end I found that Xvnc was less reliable on the Alpha than it was on a
P3 or P4, so I switched over to using my laptop.  Pentium is the most
thoroughly tested Linux platform, period.

The 500 MHz Alpha will blow away your old P2 in terms of performance.

Sorry I don't know where on the net to get Redhat for Alpha.  I copied the
CDs from a co-worker.

