On my 500, the graphics is integral to the motherboard.  I get a similar CXT
error.  A replacement motherboard was not cost effective for me, so my fix was
to install a PMAGB-B.  The system will use an add-in card for the console, if
one is present.

Afterward, Tru64 UNIX would come up with two screens, so I disabled the
onboard controller in the kernel.  I think I also made some NVRAM changes to
tell the machine to boot up regardless of the CXT error.

