On Mon, 4 Aug 2003, Paul Repacholi wrote:

> When did Linux get TurboChannel support?

 Well, I can't say exactly -- patches were floating around for 2.0 and the
Linus' official tree got them at 2.2.  Currently 2.4 works just fine and
the forthcoming 2.6 should work soon, too (there's a minor nit in the time
handling code due to a recent unification).  For best result either grab
the kernel from the MIPS CVS (http://www.linux-mips.org/) or use Debian --
development isn't done in the Linus' tree and synchronizations happen only
every once and then.

 Due to the lack of appropriate hardware, there is no support for TC
systems other than MIPS-based DECstations.

